.TH b4-categories-list 1  "b4 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
b4\-categories\-list \- List categories
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBb4 categories list\fR [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-header\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List categories
.PP
List the category catalogue as a tree, with the number and the sum of the bookings in each category.
.PP
The levels of a category are the parts of its name between colons: `Wohnen:Nebenkosten:Strom` is `Strom` below `Nebenkosten` below `Wohnen`. Table output indents each level by two blanks. A parent that is no category of its own, only the beginning of another name, is listed with the note `no record`. Categories of one level are ordered by name, ignoring case, character by character in Unicode order: digits and punctuation come before letters, and letters outside A to Z, such as umlauts, after Z.
.PP
BOOKINGS and SUM are the bookings of the category itself and their net sum (credits minus debits); WITH CHILDREN and SUM WITH CHILDREN include all categories below it. Every booking counts once: a split booking or a collective booking counts as its parts, not as parts plus the whole. Pending bookings are included. Sums are per currency: a category with bookings in several currencies has one line for each. A booking belongs to the category of the same name, ignoring case.
.PP
Bookings in a category that is not in the catalogue follow under `(not in catalogue)`, one entry per name (ignoring case), and bookings without a category under `(uncategorized)`. BOOKINGS over all lines is therefore the number of all bookings that count.
.PP
The other formats have one row per category and currency, with these columns: `full_name`, `name` (the last level), `parent` (the full name of the parent), `depth` (0 at the top), `kind` (`category`, `implied_parent` for a parent that is no category of its own, `not_in_catalogue` or `uncategorized`), `currency`, `booking_count`, `sum`, `booking_count_with_children`, `sum_with_children`, and from the `categories` table `budget_period`, `budget_amount`, `special`, `totals_bucket` and `hidden_by_banking4`. A category without bookings has one row with no currency and no sums.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: ./b4.duckdb]
Database file: written by `decrypt`, read by every other command
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBB4_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format [default: table]

table is made for reading: line breaks, control characters and text direction overrides in the data are replaced. csv, jsonl and json are data: written to a file or a pipe they are exact, byte for byte. Only when they are written to a terminal are the characters a terminal acts on (escape sequences, text direction overrides) made harmless: csv shows U+FFFD in their place, json and jsonl write them as \\uXXXX escapes.

In json and jsonl a number that a double cannot hold exactly is a string of its digits: an integer beyond 2^53, a decimal of more than 15 significant digits.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Aligned text, fitted to the terminal
.IP \(bu 2
json: One JSON array of objects
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl: One JSON object per line
.IP \(bu 2
csv: Comma\-separated values with a header line
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-header\fR
Leave out the header line of table and csv output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Do not print informational messages to stderr

Silences progress and summary lines and the "no rows" note. Warnings and errors are still printed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
b4 categories list
    Show the category tree with counts and sums.
b4 categories list \-\-output jsonl
    One JSON object per category and currency.
b4 categories list \-\-output csv | grep \(aq,uncategorized,\(aq
    The number and the sum of the bookings without a category.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBb4\fR(1),
